                <td width=572 valign=center colspan=10 style="width:343.6000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:none;
mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>This course provides a comprehensive introduction to the fundamental theories, core methodologies, and clinical applications of Child Life. Designed to develop students’ competencies in psychological support for pediatric patients, the curriculum focuses on reducing medical anxiety and improving treatment adherence through evidence-based approaches. Key components include foundational theories of child development; Specialized physician-patient communication techniques; Therapeutic medical play interventions; Tailored psychological strategies for diverse medical conditions. The course also examines cutting-edge applications of artificial intelligence in Child Life, fostering interdisciplinary innovation. Utilizing case-based learning, clinical simulations, and interactive pedagogy, the program enhances practical skills while cultivating medical humanism. By integrating theoretical knowledge with hands-on experience, we prepare compassionate healthcare professionals equipped with both technical expertise and emotional intelligence to deliver child-centered care.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
